# The Python fronts carry their OWN copy of every C source by design, and the .Rcheck trees are
# build output. Both are mirrors: left in, each C routine appears two or three times and every
# query returns duplicates. Exclude the copies and keep the R package sources as the single truth;
# the parity harnesses are what verify the copies agree.
arcstat-py/src/arcstat/*.c
arcstat-py/src/arcstat/*.h
ellstat-py/src/ellstat/*.c
ellstat-py/src/ellstat/*.h
*.Rcheck/
graphify-out/
dist/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
.git/
